# m9m Server Access (shared infra)

## SSH details (as of 2026-09-04)

The deploy target is the shared development server at `187.77.113.218`.
SSH is **not** on port 22 — port 22 is firewalled. The live SSH listener is on
**port 2212**.

```bash
ssh -p 2212 root@187.77.113.218
```

Confirmed working credentials: `root` with the SSH key in
`C:\Users\HYPE R Series\.ssh\id_rsa` (RSA passphrase protected — agent must be
loaded with `ssh-add` first if a passphrase is set).

## Open ports on the server (verified 2026-09-04)

- 22    — closed (firewalled)
- 80    — open (HTTP)
- 443   — open (HTTPS)
- 2212  — SSH (use this for shell access)
- 5678  — n8n editor UI + webhook ingress
- 8080  — m9m backend + webhook ingress
- 9090  — m9m metrics (if running with metrics enabled)

## Deploy workflow

The deployed m9m binary is built from this repository (`github.com:maharsolution/m9m.git`).
The full pipeline is:

1. **Local:** commit + push changes
   ```bash
   git add -A
   git commit -m "fix: ..."
   git push origin main
   ```

2. **Server:** SSH in, pull, rebuild the Docker image, restart the stack.
   ```bash
   ssh -p 2212 root@187.77.113.218
   cd /opt/m9m        # adjust path if different on the box
   git pull
   docker compose build m9m-backend
   docker compose up -d m9m-backend
   ```

   The project already ships a `docker-compose.yml` (m9m-backend +
   n8n-designer-frontend + mysql-db + postgres-db). Only `m9m-backend`
   needs to be rebuilt — `m9m` is built FROM source in the project's
   `Dockerfile` (Go 1.24 alpine + CGO for sqlite3), so no pre-built image
   push is required.

3. **Verify:**
   ```bash
   curl http://187.77.113.218:8080/healthz
   curl http://187.77.113.218:8080/api/v1/node-types | jq '.[].name' | grep xml
   python scripts/test-parity-sheet.py --phase post
   ```

## Why the rule exists

On 2026-09-04 the first deploy attempt timed out for ~10 minutes because
the agent assumed port 22 was open (it isn't). The user had to intervene
with the correct port (`2212`). Always use `-p 2212` and prefer
`StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new` on first connection.
